  "explanation": {
    "markdown": "## Passive voice in the different verb tenses\n\nTo make a passive verb form, we have to use **be** in a particular verb tense and add the **past participle** of the main verb after it. You can see how to use the passive voice with different [verb tenses](https://test-english.com/grammar-points/b1/review-verb-tenses-b1/) below.  \n  \n![Passive verb forms – all tenses](/uploads/grammar/b1/passive-verb-forms/img-1.png)\n\n## Active and passive\n\nIn a [passive sentence](https://test-english.com/grammar-points/a2/present-past-simple-passive/), the object of an active sentence becomes the subject. In a passive voice sentence, the subject is the receiver of the action, not the doer of the action.\n\n‣ *They take the photos in Africa*. (active)\n\n‣ *The photos are taken in Africa.* (passive)",
